+// and in a mixed vector an opaque lane falls out of the general arithmetic
+// (dest_alpha = 255, ratio = 255, AlphaMerge(..., 255) returns the source),
+// so every lane matches the scalar path exactly:
+//   - dest.alpha == 0        -> dest = src (rgb + src alpha)
+//   - src.alpha == 0         -> dest unchanged
+//   - src.alpha == 255       -> dest = src rgb, alpha 255
+//   - otherwise              -> dest_alpha = AlphaUnion(dest.alpha, src.alpha)
+//                               ratio = floor(src.alpha * 255 / dest_alpha)
+//                               rgb = AlphaMerge(dest, src, ratio)
+// The branches become masks. The variable division is computed with a
+// float32 division plus two integer corrections: the operands are integers
+// (numerator <= 65025), f32 division has relative error <= 2^-24, so the
+// truncated quotient is within one of the exact floor, and the corrections
+// make it exact (verified exhaustively for every reachable input pair).
+// All /255 divisions use the exact shift trick; every 16-bit intermediate
+// stays below 65281.
+//
+// For an FPDF_REVERSE_BYTE_ORDER destination (FX_RGBA_STRUCT, RGBA byte
+// order) the loaded source pixels are channel-swapped once by an
+// i8x16.swizzle that leaves the alpha bytes in place; the arithmetic
+// operates per channel and the scalar loop assigns field by field, so the
+// swap commutes with it and the lanes stay bit-identical to the scalar
+// path for either destination order.
